id: pmc-vbft
title: sync-version could silently restamp the wrong version literal during a release
description: "syncExtensionVersion replaced the first match of an unanchored version regex in src/extension.ts. Only one such literal exists today, so nothing is currently corrupted, but the moment any earlier version: string appears - a flag description, a help example - the release job would stamp that string instead. Because the damage is written by the release job rather than by a reviewed diff, it would survive every review. The match is now required to be unique, turning a silent mis-stamp into a loud failure."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: "area:release",regression-guard,safety
created_at: "2026-08-02T07:34:13.001Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T07:34:47.735Z"
deadline: "2026-08-31T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T07:34:47.718Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T07:34:47.718Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "A file with two version: literals aborts the sync with a message naming both and leaves the file unmodified; a file with none still reports the missing literal; the single-literal case stamps exactly as before"
resolution: syncExtensionVersion now requires exactly one version literal and aborts otherwise
expected_result: An ambiguous extension file aborts the release rather than stamping the wrong literal
actual_result: Two-literal fixture aborts and leaves the file unmodified; single-literal path unchanged
